---
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLIC_EMAIL } from '../config';
import { phoneAvailable } from '../lib/phone';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Accessibility', href: '/accessibility/' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility | Mr Wallcover"
  description="How the Mr Wallcover site is built for keyboard, mobile and reduced-motion use. WCAG 2.2 AA is the target. This page is not a certificate."
  path="/accessibility/"
  extraSchema={[breadcrumbNode(crumbs)]}
>
  <div class="container-page py-16">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />
    <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
    <h1 class="m-0 text-[clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4rem)]">Using this site</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>The target is WCAG 2.2 AA. This page is not a certification, and an automated check is not a finished audit.</p>
      <p>Pages use headings, visible keyboard focus and controls that can be used without dragging.{phoneAvailable && ' The phone number stays hidden until you ask for it.'} Menus close with Escape. If motion or blur is a problem, use “Reduce visual effects” in the footer, or your system’s reduced-motion setting.</p>
      <p>The material studio is optional. If WebGL is unavailable, the photograph and the written notes remain.</p>
      <p>Last checked 22 October 2026. We ran automated axe-core checks on 13 pages and tabbed through a sample of them with the keyboard, at phone width (390 pixels) and desktop width (1440 pixels).</p>
      <p>The problems found then have been corrected: on phones, keyboard focus could sit behind the bottom bar; error messages in the enquiry form were not linked to their fields; and two side panels on guide pages had no separate names for screen readers. Apart from those, the automated checks reported no violations on the pages checked.</p>
      <p>Known limitation: the enquiry form needs JavaScript to send. Without it, the form says so, and you can email {PUBLIC_EMAIL} with the same details instead.</p>
      <p>If something blocks you, email {PUBLIC_EMAIL} and say which page. We will help with the enquiry directly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
